{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Population trends for CI. Test history is one test over calendar days, from the daily JUnit rollup of every E2E run; the overview is pass rate, duration and failure mix for every run. Each panel names its population and its window. There is no single-run detail here: the run index and the run-evidence dashboards own that, and the source SHA in the rollup table links to the commit's runs on GitHub.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Run index (ci-observe)",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/ci-observe-runs-home/ci-observe-e28094-test-runs"
    },
    {
      "title": "One run's evidence (ci-observe)",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/ci-observe-run-evidence/ci-observe-e28094-run-evidence"
    },
    {
      "title": "GitHub Actions runs (osac)",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "https://github.com/osac-project/osac/actions"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "What this page answers, and which population",
      "description": "The population each section reads, and the window each section covers. They are never drawn on one axis.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Test history reads all jobs** (every E2E run, captured or not) from the daily JUnit rollup that `ci_observe_trends.py` writes to `trends.db`. Its window is the **Days** variable, not the time picker: the rollup holds one row per day, and a day only exists for runs whose GitHub artifact still existed when the rollup ran. Artifacts live 7 days.\n\n**Overview reads all jobs** twice: overall job and run numbers come from the central Prometheus `github_actions_*` metrics, and the failure mix comes from the workflow exporter. Its window is the dashboard time range.\n\nTest history is per **test id** over calendar days. It is not a single run: to read one run, open it from the run index (linked in the header).\n\nA test counts as failed when its JUnit testcase holds `<failure>` or `<error>`. A skipped test is neither a pass nor a failure and is left out of both counts."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Test history \u2014 one test, all jobs, last $days days",
      "description": "Is this test flaky, slower, or newly broken? Outcomes and durations for one test id, from the daily JUnit rollup.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Passes and failures, all jobs, last $days days \u2014 $test",
      "description": "One point per day for the selected test id. Population: all jobs that produced a JUnit artifact, captured or not. Window: the Days variable (the rollup's own calendar), not the time picker. Leave Test empty and every test's rows are drawn on the same day; set it to one test id for a readable line.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "workflow-api"
